<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lasta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lasta is a mountainous historic region of north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amhara">Amhara</a> Region, centred on the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalibela">Lalibela</a>. It was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Agaw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagwe-dynasty">Zagwe dynasty</a>, which ruled Ethiopia from about the 12th century until 1270. Its later rulers, the wagshums of Wag and Lasta, claimed descent from the Zagwe kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lasta.jpg" alt="Lasta" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Varavour · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Ethiopia,_before_1935.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
